GnomeAI-RS for Debian
=====================

The package is installed by an administrator, but the application always runs
as the desktop user. Do not launch it with sudo.

The desktop menu entry and these compatible commands open the same native GUI:

  gnomeai-rs /path/to/workspace
  gnomef-rs /path/to/workspace
  gnomef-agent /path/to/workspace

Microsoft .NET SDK 8.0.424, including the .NET 8 runtime used by Avalonia, is
bundled privately under `/usr/lib/gnomeai-rs/dotnet`. No Microsoft APT source
or separate `dotnet-sdk-8.0` package is required. The bundled SDK is added to
`DOTNET_ROOT` and `PATH` only for GnomeAI-RS and its child processes.

Runtime state and API keys use owner-only permissions under:

  ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/gnomeai-rs

The sidebar exposes workspace, provider, model, Web Search and sandbox
selection. `normal` asks for approval before host-side mutations,
`full-access` skips ordinary user-level prompts, and `read-only` blocks
mutations. Root commands still use a separate approval and masked credential
dialog.

WhatsApp is configured from the native sidebar. Pairing state and the QR code
are shown inside the GUI; the packaged private loopback helper has no browser
page or public launcher. Its per-user service starts automatically at login
and remains active when the Avalonia window is closed:

  systemctl --user status gnomeai-whatsapp.service
  systemctl --user restart gnomeai-whatsapp.service

The service and UI share a protected token stored under the user's GnomeAI
state directory. It is never installed as a system-wide credential.

Managed SKILL.md packages live under:

  ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/gnomeai-rs/skills

The packaged Firecrawl helper remains lazy and rootless:

  gnomeai-firecrawl status
  gnomeai-firecrawl logs
  gnomeai-firecrawl stop

The former `gnomef-web`, `gnomeai-webtool` and static browser page are no
longer installed.
